# Force LF line endings in the repository and in your working copy.
#
# You are on Windows. Without this, Git may check files out with CRLF line
# endings. A shell script with CRLF fails inside a Linux container or on an
# EC2 instance with errors like "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" or
# "$'\r': command not found", and the cause is invisible in most editors.
# This one line prevents that whole class of problem.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary files.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary
